WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.680
Peace be upon you, and welcome to the third video of Module Two of our fellowship.

2
00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:15.460
In the last video, we asked why people get sick, and discovered the story isn't just genetics and prescriptions. Today, we dive deeper to uncover the hidden forces shaping our health without us realizing.

3
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:22.880
Let's ask ourselves a vital question: Are all humans truly born with equal opportunities to live a healthy, thriving life?

4
00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.400
Assume in good faith that we all started from the exact same starting line...

5
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.280
...and that each person holds their own destiny and bodily choices in their hands.

6
00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:33.560
Yet the reality we witness on the street tells a completely different story.

7
00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:36.880
The city where you open your eyes, the neighborhood where you grow up...

8
00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:39.580
...the roof sheltering you, and your parents' level of education...

9
00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:41.960
...the income entering your pocket at the end of the month...

10
00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:44.100
...none of these are trivial marginal details.

11
00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:46.640
These are the genuine forces shaping your health.

12
00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:51.180
In public health, we call them the Social Determinants of Health.

13
00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:54.880
The World Health Organization summarized these determinants in simple words:

14
00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:59.800
They are the conditions in which we are born, grow, live, work, and age.

15
00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:03.560
Health isn't forged solely in doctor offices and emergency rooms.

16
00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:07.660
Real health is cooked in home kitchens by the quality of available food...

17
00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:12.480
...in school playgrounds, ventilation levels, occupational safety, and neighborhood cleanliness.

18
00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.520
Let's take education as an example:

19
00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:19.640
Education isn't merely a framed certificate hanging on a wall to take photos with and please our mothers.

20
00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:21.580
Education is a genuine protective shield.

21
00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:24.120
It enables you to read food nutrition labels...

22
00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:25.740
...understand what hydrogenated fats mean...

23
00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:27.640
...comprehend preventive guidelines...

24
00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:30.200
...and opens doors to stable, safe employment.

25
00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:31.520
Investing in education...

26
00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:33.940
...is a direct investment in the arteries of society.

27
00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:35.600
From here, we arrive...

28
00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:37.280
...at income and financial capability.

29
00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:40.060
Imagine a father who understands the hazards of fried foods...

30
00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:41.060
...and processed oils...

31
00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:43.500
...longing to provide his children daily fresh fruits...

32
00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:44.520
...salmon, and avocados.

33
00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:48.760
Yet when he opens his wallet, he finds only echoes and economic drought.

34
00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:51.280
So he is forced to buy cheap, filling food...

35
00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:53.080
...potatoes and bread...

36
00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:54.900
...just to stave off his children's hunger.

37
00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:56.720
The issue here isn't a lack of awareness...

38
00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.580
...nor that this man doesn't care for his children's well-being.

39
00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:03.160
The obstacle is harsh economic constraint slamming the door on healthy alternatives.

40
00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:06.380
When a kilo of apples costs as much as a barrel of oil...

41
00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:09.120
...how do you expect to convince people to eat five fruit servings a day?

42
00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:19.980
Looking beyond money, we find factors like housing, work environments, and social support: damp, overcrowded homes deprived of sunlight create fertile ground for asthma and respiratory illnesses...

43
00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:23.860
...compared to well-ventilated homes fronting green spaces where children can play.

44
00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:31.360
Workplace stress, grueling shifts, indignity, and job insecurity leave a heavy toll, elevating blood pressure and glycemic levels.

45
00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:37.960
Even social support—family and friends who comfort you—operates like an invisible psychological dispensary...

46
00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:42.100
...giving you resilience against despair, strokes, and the strains of life.

47
00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.660
To anchor this in reality...

48
00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:46.120
...let's hear the story of two people in their forties.

49
00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:48.480
Both turned forty on the exact same day...

50
00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.780
...and both began developing hypertension.

51
00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:53.000
The first is highly educated...

52
00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:54.620
...with an excellent, stable income...

53
00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:57.360
...living in a tranquil neighborhood with time for afternoon walks...

54
00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.140
...holding comprehensive health insurance...

55
00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:01.140
...with a supportive family providing peace of mind.

56
00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:02.680
He is well protected.

57
00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:05.800
The second works two grueling jobs that grind him down...

58
00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:08.920
...returning late at night to a crowded, polluted district...

59
00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:11.160
...drowning in debts keeping him awake...

60
00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:13.120
...with no one around to listen or offer support.

61
00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:17.280
Are you surprised that disease will progress far worse in the second man?

62
00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.420
They can never be on equal footing.

63
00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:21.240
The first possesses socioeconomic shields defending him...

64
00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:24.800
...while the second stands stripped and exposed before illness.

65
00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:26.760
And this narrative leads us to a painful reality:

66
00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:29.160
Climate change is never neutral.

67
00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:31.500
The climate does not strike everyone with equal fairness.

68
00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:35.240
On the contrary, it unleashes its harshest blows upon the most vulnerable.

69
00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:42.180
Imagine a suffocating heatwave: the affluent sit in air conditioning with cold water in hand, totally shielded from the heat...

70
00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:48.380
...while construction and farm laborers labor under a sun hot enough to split stone just to earn their daily bread...

71
00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:52.600
...returning home to zinc-sheet roofs without air conditioning or even a fan.

72
00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:57.840
When freshwater dwindles, impoverished quarters are the first to suffer thirst and water contamination.

73
00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.140
Climate change here is not merely elevated temperature...

74
00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:02.180
...it is an amplifier of social injustice.

75
00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:05.520
This brings us to the true compass of the health educator:

76
00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:07.500
Treat the etiology, not just the symptom.

77
00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:11.560
Instead of preaching canned, patronizing advice to people...

78
00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:15.420
'Everyone, you must relax, eliminate stress, and join a gym!'

79
00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:17.820
The smart educator pauses and asks:

80
00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:20.820
Are gym memberships and nutritious foods even attainable for these people?

81
00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:22.360
What circumstances are suffocating them?

82
00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:26.540
The goal is designing realistic initiatives rooted in compassion and structural empathy...

83
00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:29.760
...rather than airborne preachments that amplify their helplessness and guilt.

84
00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:31.600
In conclusion, reflect with us on this question:

85
00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:38.240
What socioeconomic determinants drive people in your community toward health complications like smoking or diabetes?

86
00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:41.260
Reflecting on this inquiry unlocks genuine transformation.

87
00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:44.840
In Video Four, we will transition together to field evaluation tools...

88
00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:47.860
...how to accurately monitor and quantify these challenges across our neighborhoods...

89
00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:50.560
...to build successful community health interventions on the ground.

90
00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:53.040
Thank you for watching, and see you in the next video!
